'''Guadalajara''' ({{IPAc-en|ˌ|ɡ|w|ɑː|d|əl|ə|ˈ|h|ɑːr|ə}} {{respell|GWAH|də|lə|HAR|ə}} {{IPA-bl|ɡwaðalaˈxaɾa|lang}}; {{Langx|tpn|Itáwára|4=stone place}}) is an urban [[Communes of Balisca|commune]] within the [[Guarapiranga]] [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Hesperia]]. It is located in the northern extremity of the [[Guarapiranga Valley]]. In the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]] it recorded a population of 482,754 people, making it Hesperia's x-most populous commune.

The commune is named after {{lang|es|[[w:Guadalajara, Spain|Guadalajara]]|italic=no}}, [[W:Spain|Spain]], which is derived from [[W:Andalusi Arabic|Andalusi Arabic]] {{lang|ar|وادي الحجارة}} ({{lang|ar-Latn|wādī al-ḥajārah}}), which means 'Valley of the Stones', or 'Fortress Valley'. 

